      "id": "opencode-repeated-literal-call-id-is-unverifiable-under-the-global-rule",
      "driver": "opencode",
      "target_bundle_id": "testing-strategy",
      "note": "Observed on a real host: a short literal call id is reused for skill invocations in different sessions, naming different skills. This contract requires ids unique across all skill invocations, so a record carrying the collision is unverifiable rather than a pass. Pinning it here keeps the open scope decision visible instead of letting an extractor silently pick a rule.",
      "transcript": [
        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "skill",
          "callID": "skill_0",
          "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"name": "testing-strategy"}}
        },
        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "skill",
          "callID": "skill_0",
          "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"name": "defect-diagnosis"}}
        },
        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "task",
          "callID": "call_sanitizedTask",
          "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {}}
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "schema_version": 1,
        "event_contract_version": "skill-events-v2",
        "event_contract_status": "stable",
        "skill_events_available": true,
        "task_tool_events_available": true,
        "first_task_tool_event_index": 2,
        "event_index_source": "fixture-modeled-single-monotonic-stream",
        "skills_invoked": [
          {
            "skill": "testing-strategy",
            "event_index": 0,
            "tool_use_id": "skill_0",
            "matching_tool_result": true,
            "completed": true
          },
          {
            "skill": "defect-diagnosis",
            "event_index": 1,
            "tool_use_id": "skill_0",
            "matching_tool_result": true,
            "completed": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_matched_call": {
        "decision": "deny",
        "reason_code": "event_contract_unverifiable"
      },
      "open_decision": "tool_use_id_uniqueness_scope"
    },
    {
      "id": "codex-cli-skill-md-read-is-observable-but-unregistered",
      "driver": "codex-cli",
      "target_bundle_id": "ccl-skills:testing-strategy",
      "observed_mechanism": "This driver has no skill tool. Its session advertises skills with a root-alias table and instructs the agent to read the skill's SKILL.md before acting, so an invocation appears as a generic tool call whose arguments name <declared skill root>/<name>/SKILL.md. That is observable, but registering it needs a typed exception to the argument-exclusion rule, a rule separating skill-root reads from ordinary repository file reads, and defined de-duplication for repeat reads. Until those are decided, this driver stays unregistered.",
      "transcript": [
        {
          "type": "response_item",
          "payload": {
            "type": "custom_tool_call",
            "call_id": "call_sanitized",
            "name": "exec",
            "status": "completed",
            "input": "read_file(\"<skill-root>/testing-strategy/SKILL.md\")"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "response_item",
          "payload": {"type": "custom_tool_call_output", "call_id": "call_sanitized"}
        }
      ],
      "degradation": {
        "status": "invocation_unverifiable",
        "reason": "driver_shape_unregistered"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cursor-agent-has-no-skill-tool-and-no-grounded-invocation-evidence",
      "driver": "cursor-agent",
      "target_bundle_id": "testing-strategy",
      "observed_mechanism": "This driver records paired tool-call and tool-result objects linked by a call id, which would map cleanly, but its recorded tool set carries no skill tool: the observed names are shell, file read, edit, search, todo and task tools only. Its skill trees exist on disk, so an invocation would again have to be inferred from a file read of a SKILL.md under a skill root. On the inspected host the few such reads target other hosts' skill trees during ordinary repository work, so there is no grounded invocation evidence to author a known answer from. Unregistered for lack of evidence, not by assumption.",
      "transcript": [
        {
          "type": "tool-call",
          "toolCallId": "call_sanitized",
          "toolName": "Read",
          "args": {"path": "<other-host-skill-root>/some-skill/SKILL.md"}
        },
        {
          "type": "tool-result",
          "toolCallId": "call_sanitized",
          "toolName": "Read",
          "result": "<sanitized>"
        }
      ],
      "degradation": {
        "status": "invocation_unverifiable",
        "reason": "driver_shape_unregistered"
      }
    },
